=== REASONING ===
ADR-015 invariant preservation:

I1 default-off — registry entry sets DefaultOn: false. The
    feature is opt-in even after the user enables ai_mode.

I3 baseline intact — GrafanaPanelPage renders the deterministic
    manual JSON editor + curated catalog viewer + Copy-to-clipboard
    button regardless of AI feature toggle state. The baseline
    is the canonical view; the AI section is layered alongside.
    The page never auto-applies an LLM proposal.

I4 zero egress — The strategy uses the canonical decorator
    chain (redaction → rate limit → cost cap → audit → trace)
    inherited from the F5 dispatcher. No raw provider client
    is referenced from feature code. PolicyAlertBuilder is
    used per the slice prompt.

I5 hidden UI — AINLGrafanaPanel is wrapped in
    withAiFeature('nl-grafana-panel', InnerSection). When the
    feature is not enabled (off-mode OR per-feature toggle off),
    the HOC returns null and the section is entirely absent
    from the DOM. The off-mode invariant test asserts both
    branches.

I6 404 routes — POST /api/v1/ai/power/grafana-panel/draft is
    wrapped with ai.GuardedHandler('nl-grafana-panel', ...) by
    the canonical mountAIRoutes wiring in internal/api/ai_routes.go.
    The Go-side TestNLGrafanaPanelAIOffManualEditorWorks proves
    the route returns 404 when ai_mode='off'.

I7 per-feature opt-in — registry key + per-feature toggle must
    BOTH be on. The off-mode invariant test exercises both
    halves (mode=off+toggle=true → hidden; mode=cloud+toggle=false
    → hidden; mode=cloud+toggle=true → visible).

I10 type-system — every backend mutation goes through the
    typed F4 tool framework (draft_grafana_panel +
    validate_grafana_panel). The LLM never gets a free-form
    write path. The frontend's parseGrafanaPanelDraft validates
    the typed payload before exposing it via onApply.

I12 client/bg — the slice declares one chunk
    (`ai-nl-grafana-panel`) and one storage key
    (`ai.grafanaPanel.draft`) in the registry RouteSet metadata.
    The off-mode invariant test asserts the storage key is not
    written to in off mode (the page never mounts the AI
    drafter at all in off mode, so neither setItem call paths
    are reachable).

P10 baseline coexistence: GrafanaPanelAssistant selection is
    `ai_mode != 'off' && ai_features['nl-grafana-panel']`, gated
    inside withAiFeature; the manual JSON editor remains the
    canonical baseline for off-mode users.

P11/P12 wired-or-absent: AINLGrafanaPanel imports useAiStream
    and POSTs against /ai/power/grafana-panel/draft; the
    "Draft panel" button's disabled prop is COMPUTED
    (`!canDraft` where canDraft = !isStreaming && hasPrompt);
    no placeholder strings remain (W1 scan = 0).

HX (Helix UX): the AI surface renders through AIFeatureCard
    with buttonLabel='Draft panel' (the per-feature verb,
    NOT 'Ask Helix'). The card paints "Ask Helix · Draft
    panel" as the visible label. On-mode wiring test uses
    UNANCHORED regex /Draft panel/i.

Per-request scope binding (defense-in-depth, beyond AI-off):
    nl_grafana_panel.go's WithGrafanaPanelScope binds the
    in-scope panel-types, datasource-types, and tables into
    the request context. checkGrafanaPanelScopeAndShape rejects
    any panel type, datasource type, or referenced table outside
    the scope; checkPostgresTargetSQL rejects any non-SELECT/WITH
    rawSql or any reference to an out-of-scope table. The
    refusal_unknown_panel_type and refusal_write_query goldens
    pin the canned-response refusal contract.

Tables source-of-truth: nlGrafanaPanelCuratedTables is an alias
    for nlSqlPlaygroundCuratedCatalog. The same five tables
    (drives, charging_sessions, vehicles, alerts,
    signal_log_view) are exposed. Any future slice that adds a
    table to the catalog updates a single declaration.

Postgres rawSql contract reuses 0057's primitives:
    readonlySQLForbiddenKeywords (15-keyword deny list),
    readonlySQLPrefixRe (SELECT/WITH only), readonlySQLKeywordRe
    (whole-word match for the deny list),
    extractReferencedTables (table-name extractor). No
    duplicate write paths; same single-source-of-truth.

